Labeled formal units asserted in the argument — theorems, proofs, definitions, and the definitional structures.

<section #ag-corollary | `<corollary>`>

Compiles to eHTML `<corollary>`.

<code #code:ag-corollary-1>
<corollary | Every prime greater than 2 is odd.>
</code>

<minipage #mp:ag-corollary-1>
<corollary | Every prime greater than 2 is odd.>
</minipage>

</section>

<section #ag-dd | `<dd>`>

Compiles to eHTML `<dd>`.

<code #code:ag-dd-1>
<dd | An academic publishing system built on HTML+CSS+JS.>
</code>

<minipage #mp:ag-dd-1>
<dd | An academic publishing system built on HTML+CSS+JS.>
</minipage>

*A definition-list description. Appears as a child of &lt;dl&gt;,
following the term it defines.*

</section>

<section #ag-definition | `<definition>`>

Compiles to eHTML `<definition>`.

<code #code:ag-definition-1>
<definition | A *group* is a set with an associative binary operation, identity, and inverses.>
</code>

<minipage #mp:ag-definition-1>
<definition | A *group* is a set with an associative binary operation, identity, and inverses.>
</minipage>

</section>

<section #ag-dl | `<dl>`>

Compiles to eHTML `<dl>`.

<code-block #code:ag-dl-1>
<dl>
  <dt | enscribe>
  <dd | An academic publishing system built on HTML+CSS+JS.>
  <dt | eHTML>
  <dd | The canonical semantic HTML vocabulary.>
  <dt | Enscribe shorthand>
  <dd | The shorthand authoring syntax that compiles to eHTML.>
</dl>
</code-block>

<minipage #mp:ag-dl-1>
<dl>
  <dt | enscribe>
  <dd | An academic publishing system built on HTML+CSS+JS.>
  <dt | eHTML>
  <dd | The canonical semantic HTML vocabulary.>
  <dt | Enscribe shorthand>
  <dd | The shorthand authoring syntax that compiles to eHTML.>
</dl>
</minipage>

*Long-form &lt;dl&gt; with short-form &lt;dt&gt;/&lt;dd&gt; children. The natural
authoring pattern.*

</section>

<section #ag-dt | `<dt>`>

Compiles to eHTML `<dt>`.

<code #code:ag-dt-1>
<dt | enscribe>
</code>

<minipage #mp:ag-dt-1>
<dt | enscribe>
</minipage>

*A definition-list term. Appears as a child of &lt;dl&gt;.*

</section>

<section #ag-example | `<example>`>

Compiles to eHTML `<example>`.

<code #code:ag-example-1>
<example | The integers under addition form a group.>
</code>

<minipage #mp:ag-example-1>
<example | The integers under addition form a group.>
</minipage>

</section>

<section #ag-glossary | `<glossary>`>

Compiles to eHTML `<glossary>`.

<code-block #code:ag-glossary-1>
<glossary #project-terms>
  <glossary-entry>
    <dt | enscribe>
    <dd | An academic publishing system built on HTML+CSS+JS.>
  </glossary-entry>
  <glossary-entry>
    <dt | eHTML>
    <dd | The canonical semantic HTML vocabulary.>
  </glossary-entry>
</glossary>
</code-block>

<minipage #mp:ag-glossary-1>
<glossary #project-terms>
  <glossary-entry>
    <dt | enscribe>
    <dd | An academic publishing system built on HTML+CSS+JS.>
  </glossary-entry>
  <glossary-entry>
    <dt | eHTML>
    <dd | The canonical semantic HTML vocabulary.>
  </glossary-entry>
</glossary>
</minipage>

*A glossary with two entries. Each &lt;glossary-entry&gt; uses &lt;dt&gt;/&lt;dd&gt;
for its term and definition (the same shapes &lt;dl&gt; uses), wrapped
in the entry's own envelope for cross-reference / styling.*

</section>

<section #ag-glossary-entry | `<glossary-entry>`>

Compiles to eHTML `<glossary-entry>`.

<code-block #code:ag-glossary-entry-1>
<glossary-entry #term:enscribe>
  <dt | enscribe>
  <dd | An academic publishing system built on HTML+CSS+JS.>
</glossary-entry>
</code-block>

<minipage #mp:ag-glossary-entry-1>
<glossary-entry #term:enscribe>
  <dt | enscribe>
  <dd | An academic publishing system built on HTML+CSS+JS.>
</glossary-entry>
</minipage>

*A single glossary entry. The id uses the "term:" colon-prefix
convention so cross-references like &lt;ref @term:enscribe&gt; can
resolve into the entry.*

</section>

<section #ag-lemma | `<lemma>`>

Compiles to eHTML `<lemma>`.

<code #code:ag-lemma-1>
<lemma | Every continuous function on a compact set attains its maximum.>
</code>

<minipage #mp:ag-lemma-1>
<lemma | Every continuous function on a compact set attains its maximum.>
</minipage>

</section>

<section #ag-proof | `<proof>`>

Compiles to eHTML `<proof>`.

<code-block #code:ag-proof-1>
<theorem | The sum of two even integers is even.>

<proof>
Let $a = 2m$ and $b = 2n$. Then $a + b = 2(m + n)$, which is
even. $\square$
</proof>
</code-block>

<minipage #mp:ag-proof-1>
<theorem | The sum of two even integers is even.>

<proof>
Let $a = 2m$ and $b = 2n$. Then $a + b = 2(m + n)$, which is
even. $\square$
</proof>
</minipage>

*The canonical pattern: &lt;theorem&gt; followed by sibling &lt;proof&gt;.
The proof is NOT nested inside the theorem.*

</section>

<section #ag-proposition | `<proposition>`>

Compiles to eHTML `<proposition>`.

<code #code:ag-proposition-1>
<proposition | The sum of two even integers is even.>
</code>

<minipage #mp:ag-proposition-1>
<proposition | The sum of two even integers is even.>
</minipage>

</section>

<section #ag-remark | `<remark>`>

Compiles to eHTML `<remark>`.

<code #code:ag-remark-1>
<remark | The converse does not hold in general.>
</code>

<minipage #mp:ag-remark-1>
<remark | The converse does not hold in general.>
</minipage>

</section>

<section #ag-theorem | `<theorem>`>

Compiles to eHTML `<theorem>`.

<code #code:ag-theorem-1>
<theorem | If $a^2 + b^2 = c^2$ then the triangle is right-angled.>
</code>

<minipage #mp:ag-theorem-1>
<theorem | If $a^2 + b^2 = c^2$ then the triangle is right-angled.>
</minipage>

*Short-form with pipe content. The body is parsed normally.*

</section>
